{
  "title": "SR latch",
  "group": "Electronics — digital",
  "description": "SR latch from two cross-coupled NOR gates: set pulse, hold, reset pulse, hold — bistability in 8 transistors",
  "schematic": {
    "notes": [
      {
        "x": 40,
        "y": -158,
        "title": "SR latch — what this testbench does",
        "lines": [
          "An SR latch: two cross-coupled NOR gates (N1*, N2*),",
          "8 transistors total. VS delivers a Set pulse and VR a",
          "Reset pulse; each NOR's output feeds back to the",
          "other's input, so the pair latches one of two states.",
          "Probes q (CQ) and qb (CQB) are always complementary",
          "and HOLD their value in the gaps between pulses --",
          "that memory is the bistability.",
          "",
          "Set VR.td = 3e-08 and re-run to reset earlier."
        ]
      }
    ],
